/**
 * @mainpage BMP Image Processing
 * 
 * @section intro_sec Introduction
 * This library provides functionality for working with BMP images,
 * including loading, saving, and various image processing operations.
 * 
 * @section features_sec Main Features
 * - Loading and saving BMP files
 * - Image rotation by 90 and -90 degrees
 * - Gaussian blur application
 * - Multi-threaded image processing
 * 
 * @section classes_sec Main Classes
 * - BMPFile - class for working with BMP files
 * - BMPPixelMatrix - class for working with pixel matrix
 * 
 * @section usage_sec Usage
 * Example of library usage:
 * @code
 * BMPFile image("input.bmp");
 * image.rotate90Degrees();
 * image.applyGaussianBlur();
 * image.write("output.bmp");
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @section build_sec Building
 * Requirements:
 * - g++
 * - make
 * - clang-format (for development environment)
 * 
 * To build the project, run:
 * @code
 * make
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @section run_sec Running
 * The program supports three operations:
 * 1. Clockwise rotation (`rotate-clockwise`)
 * 2. Counter-clockwise rotation (`rotate-anticlockwise`)
 * 3. Gaussian filter (`gauss`)
 * 
 * Command format:
 * @code
 * ./main <operation> <source_bmp_file> <target_bmp_file>
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @section format_sec Code Formatting
 * To format the code, run:
 * @code
 * make format
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @author Platon Lukyanov (platon_lukyanov@vk.com)
 * @version 1.0
 */ 